  "presentation_summary": [
    "29-year-old man with respiratory distress on mild exercise, dry eyes and dry mouth was diagnosed with primary Sjogren syndrome and interstitial pneumonia.",
    "At referral, vital signs were BP 120/70, pulse 78/min, RR 20/min and temperature 36.7 C; exam showed corneal erosions, decreased lacrimal secretions with 5-mm Schirmer test, xerostomia and crackles in both lung fields.",
    "Labs showed WBC 11,900/mm3, hemoglobin 10.4 g/dL, platelets 720,000/mm3, ESR 66 mm/hr, CRP 124.2 mg/L, RF 26 IU/mL, ANA 1:40 speckled, anti-SSA positive and IgG 6,224 mg/dL; CT showed cystic lesions, nodules and hilar/mediastinal lymphadenopathy."
  ],
